/*
** quaidstvpelas.src
**
** TVP-AIDS initiative, Stage 5: elasticities at a chosen period's
** (filtered or smoothed) state, reusing src/quaidselas.src's existing
** _quaidsElas() rather than hand-rolling new elasticity math -- the same
** "reuse the already-correct sibling proc" pattern this codebase already
** follows for level/variance computations.
**
** NO sslib dependency, unlike Stages 2-4: a state is accepted here as a
** plain k_states x 1 vector, not any sslib struct type, so a caller
** passes whichever column of Stage 2/3's rslt.filtered_state or Stage 4's
** a_TS it wants elasticities at -- "filtered vs. smoothed" is entirely a
** caller-side choice of which column to slice, not something this file
** needs to know about.
**
** Depends directly on src/quaidstvp.src's own quaidsTVPStateToFullB()
** (Stage 5's own recovery step -- see that proc's header) and
** src/quaidselas.src's own _quaidsElas() -- a caller must #include BOTH
** quaidstvp.src and quaidselas.src BEFORE this file, same convention as
** quaidstvpmle.src's own documented dependency on quaidstvpkalman.src.
**
** Promoted to public API in Stage 6 (was _quaidsTVPElasFit through Stage
** 5) -- real, documented, supported public API now, still not in
** package.json's src array (see CLAUDE.md's "Optional modules" section --
** sslib stays an optional adapter dependency, the same pattern
** quaidscurvature.src/pubtable_quaids.src already use, not a hard
** dependency of core estimation). In verify_package_manifest.ps1's
** intentionallyUnlisted allowlist alongside the other five TVP-AIDS
** files.
*/


/*
** quaidsTVPElasFit
**
** Purpose: income/price elasticities at one period's TVP-AIDS state,
**          via quaidsTVPStateToFullB() (state -> full n-good b matrix)
**          then _quaidsElas() (the already-correct, already-tested
**          elasticity math) -- no new elasticity formula is introduced
**          here.
**
** Format:     { er, ep, epc } = quaidsTVPElasFit(state, n1, prices, totexp, aCtl);
**
** Input:      state  -- k_states x 1 vector, one period's filtered or
**                        smoothed state (k_states = 2*n1 + n1*(n1+1)/2 --
**                        see src/quaidstvp.src's own header).
**             n1     -- number of independently-estimated equations
**                       (n = n1+1 goods total).
**             prices -- n x 1 vector of ABSOLUTE log prices (NOT the
**                       relative prices the state space itself was built
**                       from -- see CLAUDE.md's "Relative vs. absolute
**                       prices" convention note) at the evaluation point.
**             totexp -- scalar log total expenditure at the evaluation
**                       point.
**             aCtl   -- struct quaidsControl; only aCtl.alpha0 and
**                       aCtl.linear are read (see _quaidsElas()'s own
**                       header). aCtl.linear MUST be 1 -- this
**                       initiative's own Stage 1 scope decision (Stone
**                       index, no quadratic/lambda term -- see
**                       src/quaidstvp.src's own header) means
**                       quaidsTVPStateToFullB()'s output never has a
**                       lambda row for _quaidsElas() to read. A caller
**                       with no other reason to build a quaidsControl can
**                       just call quaidsControlCreate() then set
**                       aCtl.linear = 1 (aCtl.alpha0 stays its default 0).
**
** Output:     er  -- n x 1 vector of income elasticities.
**             ep  -- n x n uncompensated price elasticity matrix.
**             epc -- n x n compensated price elasticity matrix.
**
** Remarks: point elasticities only -- NO standard errors, unlike
**          quaidsElasFit()'s own delta-method SEs. Propagating the
**          reduced state's own filtered/smoothed covariance through
**          quaidsTVPStateToFullB()'s recovery step is a real, separate
**          extension (that recovery is itself linear in the state, so it
**          is tractable -- see Stage 6's own planning notes), not
**          attempted here; this proc mirrors _quaidsElas()'s own
**          point-only contract, not quaidsElasFit()'s SE-computing one,
**          by deliberate choice of which sibling proc to reuse (see this
**          file's own header).
*/
proc (3) = quaidsTVPElasFit(state, n1, prices, totexp, struct quaidsControl aCtl);
    local n, k_states, b, intcpt, er, ep, epc;

    n = n1 + 1;
    k_states = 2*n1 + n1*(n1+1)/2;

    if not aCtl.linear;
        errorlog "quaidsTVPElasFit: aCtl.linear must be 1 -- this initiative's own Stage 1 scope (Stone index, no quadratic term) means the recovered state has no lambda row for _quaidsElas() to read.";
        end;
    endif;
    if rows(state) /= k_states or cols(state) /= 1;
        errorlog "quaidsTVPElasFit: state must be a k_states x 1 vector (k_states = 2*n1 + n1*(n1+1)/2 implied by n1).";
        end;
    endif;
    if rows(prices) /= n or cols(prices) /= 1;
        errorlog "quaidsTVPElasFit: prices must be an n x 1 vector of ABSOLUTE log prices (n = n1+1), not the state space's own relative prices.";
        end;
    endif;

    b = quaidsTVPStateToFullB(state, n1);
    intcpt = 1;
    { er, ep, epc } = _quaidsElas(b, intcpt, prices, totexp, aCtl);

    retp(er, ep, epc);
endp;
